# <%~ it.instance.slug %>: High Level Design
<%
  /* WI #318 (design v2): `requires` is field-level end to end so render order
     can match the TAC HLD reference template exactly (cover block -> Problem
     Statement -> Proposed solution -> Alternatives considered -> Open
     questions -> Attachment/s).

     WI #362: this template now renders the reference's sections and nothing
     else. Affected domains, Design basis, Solution overview, Dependency list
     and Open issues are gone — the TAC template has no heading for any of
     them — and Non-functional requirements / Security and privacy are back to
     a single `##` heading each (the v1 layout), carrying only the two mandated
     NFR fields and privacy-and-confidentiality. The dropped fields still
     render in the artefacts of the stages that own them; see
     definition.yaml's `hld.requires` comment and CHANGELOG.md.

     Blank-field guard `na()` is injected once as an Eta functionHeader by
     lib/render.js (WI #273 / R2). A `module.field?` requires entry is in scope
     but not gate-blocking (WI #276), so it renders as a suppress-when-blank
     `<% if %>` section; a bare entry always renders its heading via na(). */
